 "literal": "Roaring thunder-with rainy-season-beginning united / dry-land field-of jasmine soft creeper / teeth like budding land-lord-to / sleep abandoned indeed, O friend, my eyes!",
 "translation": "The beginning of the rainy season has arrived, united with roaring thunder. In the forest clearings, the soft jasmine creepers are budding like white teeth. For the lord of this land, my eyes have completely abandoned sleep, O friend!",
 "modern": "ஒலிக்கும் இடியுடன் கார்காலம் தொடங்கிவிட்டது. முல்லை நிலத்துக் கொல்லைப் புனத்தில் உள்ள மென்மையான முல்லைக் கொடிகள் பற்களைப் போல அரும்புகளைத் தோற்றுவிக்கின்றன. அத்தகைய நாட்டின் தலைவனுக்காக, தோழியே! என் கண்கள் உறக்கத்தை இழந்துவிட்டன.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend in the mullai (forest) landscape, which is traditionally associated with patient waiting. The rainy season, which the hero promised to return by, has arrived, marked by roaring thunder. The jasmine creepers in the forest clearings are budding, and their white buds resemble beautiful teeth. Seeing these signs of the season, the heroine is filled with longing and anxiety because her lover has not yet returned. Consequently, her eyes have completely lost their sleep, and she shares her grief with her friend.",
